#
# With dEQP's transform feedback pages run in Chromium, the host's GPU engine
# is reset some 75 pages later and its Direct3D 12 device removed; every page
# after that reads back black, and QEMU ends as the next browser makes its
# first context. Chunk 6 of 2.0.1 ends so in the Debian guest under NVIDIA's
# driver 621.24 as on Rach2. Without these 29 pages it runs whole, and the 7
# pages after them that fail in Debian's reference too pass more of their
# subtests (dev-log/84-locks/84-265r.md). The host's fault is "After
# Chromium's transform feedback pages the host GPU's engine is reset pages
# later" in dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md.
chromium deqp/functional/gles3/transformfeedback/
